## Why the specialization is faithful

The new wrapper first rejects graphs containing owned `Mathlib.*` modules. It imports the exact hash-pinned authenticated overlay and changes only that imported overlay's expected owned-module set from its inherited four entries to the empty set. The inherited constructor independently recomputes the owned set from all targets and checks equality.

With the protected set empty, the inherited overlay preserves the complete official Mathlib namespace through its ordinary verified sibling links. No selected project module needs a protected Mathlib ancestor. The inherited inventory comparison, actual Lean first-namespace lookup, companion-bundle equality and refusal to replace conflicting paths still run. Missing required official artifacts still fail through the original import/compilation machinery; graph emptiness is not an assertion that every external dependency is available.

The final adapter also saves its exact wrapper bytes, wrapper hash, graph hash and empty-owned declaration in each new run before `run_targets`. The supervisor's exact body diff changes only `build_desktop.py` to `build_no_owned_mathlib.py` as the invoked child. Storage supervision and fail-closed exception handling are unchanged.

The core builder, authenticated overlay, underlying overlay, trace-transport helper and audit template all match the accepted pinned bytes. Compiler flags, resource caps, native-runtime checks, exact-context cache keys, complete audit generation and acceptance conditions are untouched. This conclusion applies to the frozen profile; future graphs require their own source/namespace review.

## Independent checks executed

The reviewer rehashed all 219 source bodies, parsed literal imports with nested-comment removal and verified the dependency order. All 217 prerequisite source/import records equal their selected records in the accepted union. Both additional source bodies remain byte-identical to the previously reviewed drafts.

For each of the 217 copied prerequisite caches, the reviewer compared the complete receipt with the accepted union's component receipt, rehashed the original receipt, reconstructed the exact-context cache key, checked the source/object identities, and verified every present object/import companion. These are successful same-executor receipts already accepted by the full union review; the unchanged builder must still recompute each current context key before reuse.

Seven controls exercised the exact inherited namespace implementation on isolated fixture directories, without constructing a builder or invoking Lean/Lake:

1. Empty-owned full-official namespace resolution and idempotence pass.
2. A changed official inventory is rejected.
3. A wrong preexisting symbolic link is rejected.
4. A conflicting real directory is rejected without replacement.
5. A missing official Mathlib namespace is rejected.
6. The exact graph guard admits an empty-owned fixture.
7. The exact graph guard rejects an owned-Mathlib fixture before wrapper construction.

